    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule: **reject creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with 409 Conflict.**\n\nFollowing the existing patterns in this Spring Boot codebase (which already had analogous rules for duplicate telephone and duplicate household):\n\n1. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, mirroring `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `rejectCityAtCapacity(...)` call into the create pipeline, plus the private helper and a `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant. It counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitively, consistent with `assignCustomerCode`) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `CityAtCapacityException` to a **409 Conflict** `ProblemDetail` with an `errors: [\"city\"]` property, matching the shape of the existing conflict handlers.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `Cp18Tests.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a fresh city to 50, then expect the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full suite is green: **29 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.",
